			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Add shutdown guard and fix static asset path resolution\n\nAdd atomic shutdown guard to Entry.rs to prevent the graceful shutdown sequence from running twice. The graceful path ends with `app_handle.exit(0)` which Tauri re-delivers as a second `ExitRequested { code: Some(0) }`. On re-entry we must NOT `prevent_exit` or spawn the shutdown task again — Cocoon has already been SIGKILLed and the second pass would log spurious \"tcp connect error\" warnings.\n\nExtend static asset path resolution in Utilities.rs to handle both `/Static/Application/` and `Static/Application/` forms. The webview's WASM loader resolves asset URLs relative to the current document, which strips the leading slash before reaching the `file:read` IPC handler. Without this fix, `tokio::fs::read` would fail with ENOENT, breaking TextMate syntax highlighting.\n\nAlso expand the benign ENOENT ignore list in DevLog.rs to suppress warnings for `.copilot/agents`, `.vscode/tasks.json`, `/User/tasks.json`, `/User/mcp.json`, `vscode-chat-images`, and `/output_<TIMESTAMP>` window log file patterns.\n\nThis prevents spurious shutdown warnings, fixes TextMate grammar loading, and reduces log noise.",
			"SHA": "bd38c344b6e75841edd53fa141b61eb9cb6a257b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T20:26:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 2 components\n\nSynchronize Mountain and Sky submodules with the following changes:\n- **Mountain:** Simplify binary naming from verbose development profile identifier to just 'Mountain'. Update Tauri identifier to 'land.editor.binary'. Remove externalBin reference to Binary/node since Node.js sidecar is now handled differently. Add vscode-file and vscode-file://vscode-app to img-src Content Security Policy for VS Code file protocol support. Delete temporary backup files (Cargo.toml.Backup, tauri.conf.json.Backup).\n- **Sky:** Add exception signature throttling to PostHog bridge — exceptions share the `$exception` event-name slot in posthog-js, so a burst of CSP refusals/console.error/unhandledrejection callbacks during workbench boot would blow through the 10/10s rate limit. Add a secondary throttle layer keyed by the first 200 chars of the error message. Both regular and exception drop counts are now reported in the `land:sky:throttle-dropped` event for visibility.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers build configuration simplification and PostHog rate limit protection while maintaining identical runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "ddf6e4aed3c5d003a92613262637479678a4a5f7"
		},
